# =============================================================================
# miaAI-lab-notes
# =============================================================================

# ---- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The skill scripts read GEMINI_API_KEY from these. Never commit them.
.env
.env.*
!.env*.example
*.key
*.pem

# ---- Upstream source repositories -------------------------------------------
# Read-only clones the book was written from. Each carries its own .git, so
# committing them here would create stray gitlinks and vendor ~11 MB of someone
# else's source. Clone them alongside this repo instead:
#   git clone https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/DeepSeek-v4-Flash-DSpark-2x-DGX-Spark
#   git clone https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks
DeepSeek-v4-Flash-DSpark-2x-DGX-Spark/
GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks/

# ---- Local tooling ----------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code skills used to author and illustrate the book. Personal tooling,
# not part of the published work. Also the home of the .env files above.
.claude/

# ---- Working notes ----------------------------------------------------------
# Repository digests, improvement plans, illustration/fidelity audits and QA
# sweeps the book was drafted from. Provenance for the numbers, not part of the
# published work.
book-notes/

# ---- LaTeX build output -----------------------------------------------------
# Everything here is regenerated by `cd book && tectonic main.tex`.
# main.pdf is the 20 MB deliverable: excluded so a rebuild-per-session habit
# does not balloon history. Ship it via a GitHub Release, or force-add a
# release cut with `git add -f book/main.pdf`.
book/main.pdf
*.aux
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.glo
*.gls
*.idx
*.ilg
*.ind
*.lof
*.log
*.lot
*.out
*.run.xml
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.xdv

# ---- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

